            <!-- Section 1: SNC Extension Pattern -->
            <section class="content-section" id="dev-architecture">
                <h2>The SNC Script Include Extension Pattern</h2>
                <p>
                    Out-of-the-box ServiceNow ITSM applications utilize the <strong>SNC Extension Pattern</strong> for Script Includes. 
                    This pattern separates read-only base platform code from customer customizations:
                </p>

                <div class="diagram-block">
                    <div class="diagram-title">SNC Script Include Inheritance Architecture</div>
                    <div class="mermaid">
                    classDiagram
                        class IncidentUtilsSNC {
                            +Boolean isMajorIncident(incidentGr)
                            +Void copyProblemWorkaround(problemGr)
                            +Void syncChildIncidents(parentGr)
                            #Read-Only Out-of-the-Box Core
                        }
                        
                        class IncidentUtils {
                            +CustomOverrideMethods()
                            #Customer Editable Override Layer
                        }
                        
                        IncidentUtilsSNC <|-- IncidentUtils : Extends via Prototype
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="info-card info-card--important">
                    <div class="info-card-title">Development Rule: Never Edit *SNC Script Includes</div>
                    <p>
                        Script Includes ending in <code>*SNC</code> (e.g. <code>IncidentUtilsSNC</code>, <code>ChangeUtilsSNC</code>) are read-only 
                        and updated automatically during family upgrades (e.g. Washington $\rightarrow$ Xanadu). 
                        To customize or override a method, add your custom implementation to the child Script Include (e.g. <code>IncidentUtils</code>).
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

